 ### [Locality-preserving Densification](9585-locality-preserving-densification.md)
-[Locality-preserving Densification](9585-locality-preserving-densification.md): Locality-preserving densification addresses the memory access throttling caused by standard Gaussian densification, where newly added primitives are appended to the end of parameter buffers, causing spatially close Gaussians to be stored far apart in memory. By reordering the Gaussian population based on 3D spatial proximity using Z-ordering (Morton order), it ensures that neighboring Gaussians in space are also adjacent in memory, thereby improving memory access coalescing. This method sets itself apart from sibling strategies like Score-based Densification by focusing on the memory layout and hardware efficiency rather than the geometric criteria for splitting or cloning primitives.
